2026-08-24T19:19:37Z	tried	what=two harness bugs found by running it, not by reading it	config=supervisor eval baseline seeded from the repo; watch refuses to start beside a live supervisor; budget gains an append-only correction record	produced=the budget read 582 evals for 308 done and now reads 308; a second supervisor is refused by name and pid instead of silently coexisting	claim=MEASURED	control=the seeding test asserts 194 from a repo that says 194 AND zero from an empty repo — a seeder that always returns the last number it saw would pass only the first half; the correction test asserts the log still has three lines, so nothing was rewritten	why=Both bugs are invisible to a reading and obvious within twenty minutes of running. The budget one is the more serious: it inflates in the direction of switching to a learned ordering too early, and it does so precisely because restart-and-resume is the system's NORMAL mode rather than an exception. Worth remembering that the harness's own instruments need the same suspicion as the project's.	node=117796
